From 2e568fba381bca9470e2df14c7029c3a402797b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:01:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] :new: Negotiate Vulkan 1.3 with the selected loader

The runtime defaults to a Vulkan 1.2 instance, which cannot enable the
core dynamic-rendering route needed by the tile-image candidate. Query
the loader already opened for window capability discovery and request
1.3 only when that loader supports it. Honor an explicit loader path and
instance-version request, and negotiate even without surface support.
Older loaders and unavailable or failed queries retain the 1.2 default;
the runtime still validates the version before creating its instance.

Add three pure regression tests covering 1.0 through 1.4 loader answers,
a missing or failed query and explicit versions that bypass the query.
All three pass. The combined candidate also passes the Android C-facade
metadata check with final runtime ffda2ffd selected through Cargo patch
configuration. This selects an instance version; it does not assert that
a physical device has the tile-image features or that a guest boots.
